{"type":"message","id":"fa9f69da","parentId":"a5f6d98a","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:01:11.589Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are extracting door schedules, finish schedules, and performing MEP coordination review for the HHC Bellevue Hospital Ambulance Drop Off project.\n\n**Project location:** /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/\n\n**REFERENCE:** Look at how USPS Greenwich did this at /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/usps-greenwich/synthesis/ — match those output formats (door_schedule_complete.json, finish_schedule_complete.json, partition_types_complete.json).\n\n**TASK 1: Door Schedule Extraction (Sheet A-701, page_021.png)**\n- Read the drawing image at drawings/pages/page_021.png AND the text layer at drawings/text/page_021.txt\n- Extract the complete door schedule: door mark, size (width x height), type, frame, hardware set, fire rating, notes\n- Extract partition types: type ID, description, STC rating, fire rating, construction layers\n- Save to synthesis/door_schedule_complete.json and synthesis/partition_types_complete.json\n- Cross-reference with specs Section 08 (Openings) from specs/specs_summary.json for hardware requirements\n\n**TASK 2: Finish Schedule Extraction (Sheet A-801, page_024.png)**\n- Read drawings/pages/page_024.png AND drawings/text/page_024.txt\n- Extract complete finish schedule: room number/name, floor finish, base, wall finish (N/S/E/W if noted), ceiling finish, ceiling height\n- Also check A-400 (page_019.png) interior elevations for additional finish info\n- Save to synthesis/finish_schedule_complete.json\n- Cross-reference with specs Divisions 09 (Finishes) for product specs\n\n**TASK 3: MEP Coordination Review**\nRead these key MEP sheets and identify coordination issues:\n\nMechanical/HVAC:\n- H-101 (page varies — check sheet_index.json) — HVAC floor plan\n- Look for ductwork routing conflicts with structural, ceiling heights vs finish schedule\n\nElectrical:\n- E-101 (page_032.png) — Power plan\n- E-201 (page_034.png) — Lighting plan  \n- E-301 (page_036.png) — Riser/panel schedules\n- Check panel capacity vs connected loads\n\nPlumbing:\n- P-101 — Plumbing floor plan\n- Check for med gas requirements (this is a hospital)\n\nFire Protection:\n- FA-101 — Fire alarm plan\n- Check ICRA impact on fire alarm/sprinkler modifications\n\nFor each discipline, read both the drawing text layer AND the image. Create:\n- synthesis/mep_coordination_review.json with findings organized by discipline\n- Flag conflicts: ceiling space conflicts, routing clashes, panel capacity issues, missing connections\n- Flag hospital-specific items: med gas, emergency power, nurse call, code blue\n\n**TASK 4: Demo Plan Analysis (Sheet AD-101, page_025.png)**\n- Extract demo scope: what's being removed\n- Cross-reference with asbestos abatement drawings (H-series) if identifiable\n- Save to synthesis/demo_scope.json\n\n**OUTPUT FORMAT:** Follow the USPS Greenwich synthesis format. All JSON should be well-structured and readable.\n\n**IMPORTANT:** Use the image tool to analyze PNG files when text layers are insufficient. Construction drawings often have info that doesn't extract well as text. For schedules especially, the image is critical.\n\nSave a summary of all findings to synthesis/extraction_summary.md when done."}],"timestamp":1770051671587}}
