ocedures:  1.  All equipment must be inspected and approved by the Owne\",\n        \"Safety Signage.  11.  Progress cleaning and waste removal.  12.  Fire prevention facilities.  13.  Barriers and fencing.  14.  Enclosures.  15.  Protection of installed work.  16.  Security.  17.  Water control.  18.  Pollution and environmental cont\",\n        \"ovide temporary partitions and ceilings as indicated on Drawings to separate work areas from  Owner occupied areas, to prevent penetration of dust and moisture into Owner occupied areas,  and to prevent damage to existing materials and equipment.  B.\"\n      ],\n      \"key_requirements\": [\n        {\n          \"category\": \"General\",\n          \"requirement\": \"NOTIFICATION OF SHUTDOWNS AND DELIVERIES:\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"category\": \"General\",\n          \"requirement\": \"PRECONSTRUCTION, SITE MOBILIZATION AND PREINSTALLATION MEETINGS\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"category\": \"Contractor Req\",\n          \"requirement\": \"give the Owner two weeks advance notice prior to all shutdown and deliveries\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"category\": \"Contractor Req\",\n          \"requirement\": \"schedule preconstruction meeting after Notice of Award for affected parties.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_number\": \"011000\",\n      \"title\": \"SUMMARY\",\n      \"division\": \"01\",\n      \"text_length\": 9911,\n      \"icra_related\": true,\n      \"icra_context\": [\n        \"nless otherwise indicated.  1.  Maintain access to existing walkways, corridors, and other adjacent occupied or used  facilities. Do not close or obstruct walkways, corridors, or other occupied or used facilities  without written permission from Owne\",\n        \"Bay Addition  1.  Project Location: 462 First Avenue, New York, NY 10016.  B.  Owner: NYC Health + Hospitals.  1.  Owner's Representative: NYC HHC | Yunjung Lee, Director Cap Bud / Con Ctrl I  212-562-7941 I Yunjung.Lee@nyc