{"type":"message","id":"a028a195","parentId":"2c5544c1","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:04:18.393Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:38","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# DOOR SCHEDULE - ED ADDITION (Drawing A-701)\n\n## Door Schedule\n\nBased on what's legible in the drawing:\n\n| Door No. | Room Name | Type | Size (W x H) | Door Material | Door Finish | Frame Material | Frame Finish | Glazing | Rating | Hardware Set | Remarks |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| ED-1-01 | CRAFT ROOM | D | 3'-0\" x 7'-0\" | HM | P | AL | NA | SAL | - | P | SAL |\n| ED-1-02 | ENTRANCE VESTIBULE | M | 6' x 4'-0\" | P | AL | NA | SAL | - | P | SAL | - |\n| ED-1-03 | MPS SECURITY FOLIO* | M | 3'-0\" x 7'-0\" | P | AL | NA | SAL | 1'-0\" x 2'-0\" | P | SAL | S5 - BALLISTIC LEVEL 3, 1 DOOR FRAME AND GLAZING |\n| ED-1-04 | MPS SECURITY FOLIO* | M | 3'-0\" x 7'-0\" | P | AL | NA | SAL | 1'-0\" x 2'-0\" | P | SAL | S5 |\n| ED-1-05 | ENTRANCE VESTIBULE | J | 1'-4\" x 4'-0\" | P | AL | NA | SAL | 12'-2 1/2\" | P | SAL | S3 |\n| ED-1-06 | ENTRANCE VESTIBULE | J | G | 3'-0\" x 7'-0\" | AL | NA | SAL | 12'-0 1/2\" | P | SAL | S5 |\n| ED-1-07 | ENTRANCE VESTIBULE | M | G | 3'-0\" x 7'-0\" | AL | NA | SAL | - | P | SAL | S3 |\n| ED-1-08 | ENTRANCE VESTIBULE | AA | 6'"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_022.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770051858387}}
{"type":"message","id":"70680aab","parentId":"a028a195","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:04:34.154Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:39","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Drawing M-101 — Mechanical Schedules\n\n**Project:** H+H Bellevue — ED Ambulance Bay Addition\n**Address:** 462 1st Avenue, New York, NY 10016\n**Architect:** ARRAY Architects\n**Contract No.:** 09/25/25\n\n---\n\n## OUTDOOR HEAT PUMP CONDENSING UNIT\n\n| Unit Tag | Location | Indoor Units Served | Cooling (MBH) | Heating (MBH) | Compressor Type | Model No. |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|---------------|---------------|-----------------|-----------|\n| ACCU-1 | Roof | See Plan | 32 | 144 | Hermetic | 73448529 |\n\n- **Basis of Design:** Trane Mitsubishi\n- Weight: 715 lbs, Gas conn: 0-1/8\", Refrigerant: 460/50/3\n- MCA: 34, MOP: 50, EER: 65.5, COP: 10, SEER: 0.48\n\n**Notes:** 10-year extended warranty, low ambient control to -4°F, provide crankcase heater, steel balls/vibration isolators, provide BIG FOOT stands.\n\n---\n\n## VRF INDOOR UNIT SCHEDULE\n\n**Basis of Design:** Trane Mitsubishi\n\n| Unit Tag | Area Served | Type | Connected To | Cooling (MBH) | Heating (MBH) | Total ESP (in.WG) |\n|----------|-------------|------|-------------|---------------|---------------|--------------------|\n| AC-1 | Cart Wash | Ducted | ACCU-1 | 30.0 | 31.7 | 882 |\n| AC-2 | Security Station | Ducted | ACCU-1 | 7.50 | 30.0 | 882 |\n| AC-3 | Entrance Vestibule | | | 5.00 | 16.0 | 763 |\n| AC-4 | NYU Security Pick-Up | | | 1.25 | 15.0 |"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_050.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770051874148}}
{"type":"message","id":"72f2fba1","parentId":"70680aab","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:04:49.792Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:40","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Fire Alarm Plan - FA-101.00\n\n## Project Information\n- **Project:** H+H Bellevue - ED Ambulance Bay Addition\n- **Location:** 462 1st Avenue, New York, NY 10016\n- **Architect:** Array Architects\n- **MEP Engineer:** Jaros Baum & Bolles (JB&B)\n- **Sheet:** FA-101.00 - Fire Alarm Floor Plan\n- **Project No:** 6629\n\n---\n\n## Drawing Contents\n\nThe sheet contains two plan views:\n\n1. **Fire Alarm Plan** (Detail 1) - Overall floor plan showing device locations\n2. **Fire Alarm Plan - FACP Location** (Detail 2) - Enlarged view showing Fire Alarm Control Panel location\n\n---\n\n## Device Locations Identified\n\n### Fire Detectors\n- **Fire Detector** noted near grid C/7 area (corridor/lobby zone)\n- **Fire Detector** noted near grid B/5 area (near entrance vestibules)\n\n### Fire Alarm Control Panel (FACP)\n- **Existing Fire Alarm Panel (FACP)** shown in Detail 2, located approximately at grid B-C / 3-2 area\n\n### Other Devices Visible\n- Multiple devices (shown as small symbols marked with **×** or squares) distributed along corridors and within spaces including:\n  - Entrance vestibules area\n  - Corridor runs\n  - Near the ambulance court area\n  - Near cart wash and support spaces\n\n### Key Spaces Referenced\n- **Ambulance Court** (grid E, 6-7)\n- **Cart Wash** (grid C, 7)\n- **Entrance Vestibules** (grid B, 6)\n- **Desserts/Station** and **Storage** (grid B, 7-8)\n- **Hose Bibb** (grid C, 8)\n- **Existing Recreation/Break Room** (grid F, 6)\n- Existing emergency canopy noted\n- New ramp with asphalt noted\n\n---\n\n## Fire Alarm System Notes (from upper right)\n\nThe notes are partially legible but include requirements such as:\n\n1. Contractor to coordinate with existing fire"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_044.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770051889764}}
